    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d524">

                <pb facs="0648" n="534" sameAs="frus:frus1924v01/pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.113/776</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Denmark</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-11-17"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                        1924</hi></date>.<lb/>[Received December 3.]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 796</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In reply to the Department’s Instruction
                    No. 226, of August 13th last,<anchor n="60" xml:id="d524-f1"/> in which
                    reference is made to an Instruction dated October 17, 1923,<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d524-f2"/> requesting this Legation to communicate to the Danish
                    Foreign Office the views of the United States Government with respect to the
                    proposed modification of the terms of the existing embargo on the shipment of
                    arms and munitions of war to China, and to express the hope of the Government of
                    the United States that the Danish Government would approve the terms of the
                    modified embargo, I have the honor to enclose, herewith, copy and translation of
                    a Note from the Royal Danish Foreign Office, dated November 6, 1924, setting
                    forth the views of the Danish Government in regard to this matter.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Oliver B.
                    Harriman</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d524-a1.xml" xpointer="d524-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
